    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d7d41d6e-e9f2-43e0-af0f-ac2146083d4f&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9203294868871_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Placement Faculty",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-01-13\n\nLocation: Harrisburg\n\nOverview We are seeking a dedicated and experienced full-time higher education nursing faculty member to join our nursing faculty team. This vital role involves coordinating clinical placement for all nursing programs, including using the document manager platform for all clinical placement required documents. In addition, this role requires a teaching component in the nursing program(s). There will be other job duties as well, including assistance with curriculum review and updating courses, being a working member of several committees and other duties as delineated by the Chief Nursing Officer/Program Lead. The ideal candidate will possess strong nursing skills, knowledge related to clinical placement, experience in teaching higher education students, knowledge and understanding of CCNE nursing essentials and competencies, and a strong commitment to excellence and support in building the nursing program. This position offers an opportunity to contribute to student outcomes while working in a dynamic university environment. Duties · Coordinate clinical placement of all nursing program students. · Collaborate with healthcare facilities and healthcare professionals to acquire clinical placements for the students. · Maintain accurate documentation of clinical placement documents and student records in the education management platform. · Assist students in uploading required documents in the education management platform. · Monitor education management platform for student completion and readiness for clinical. · Ensure all required documents, such as evaluations, are uploaded to the education management platform prior to the end of semester. · Work with platform representatives to include course learning outcomes in the education management platform. · Actively teach in the nursing program. · Other duties as requested. Experience · Proven experience in the field of nursing. · Experience in teaching at the university level. · Familiarity with nursing regulations and best practices. · Experience in clinical placement (desired). · Experience with electronic education management system (EXXAT) for clinical rotations (desired). · Prior leadership or coordination experience within a clinical setting is preferred but not required. · MSN, DNP, or PhD required.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d7d41d6e-e9f2-43e0-af0f-ac2146083d4f&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9203011316298_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Biotechnology Faculty",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-10-13\n\nLocation: Harrisburg\n\nFaculty- Professor Biotechnology (Please note this role is on-site in Harrisburg, PA)   About Harrisburg University (HU):   The Harrisburg University of Science and Technology is an independent educational institution offering innovative academic and research programs in science and technology that respond to local and global needs.   The institution fosters a diverse community of learners, provides access and support to students who want to pursue a career in science and technology, and supports business creation and economic development.   Academics at HU: Bachelor of Science (BS) degrees awarded in Analytics, Biotechnology, Computer and Information Sciences, Interactive Media, Management & eBusiness, Geospatial Technologies, and Integrative Sciences Master of Science Degrees awarded in Analytics, Biotechnology, Computer Sciences, Information Systems Engineering & Management, Learning Technologies, HCID, and Project Management BTEC Academics at HU: Harrisburg University offers a BS and MS in BTEC in addition to post BS certificates in Biomanufacturing, Medical Biotechnology, and Business and Management in Biotechnology. The program is very robust and comprehensive with sound foundational concepts in natural sciences with add-on applied concepts with ability to specialize in one/more of the following –  Food Safety and Quality Assurance, General Biotechnology, Medical Biotechnology, Nanobiotechnology, Nanobiotechnology-Nanofabrication, and Pharmaceutical Drug Design.   For more than15 years, the HU BTEC program has been the host to a Workforce Training entity - Capital Area Biotechnology Partnership (CABP,  https://www.harrisburgu.edu/capital-area-biotechnology-partnership/ ). With this in place, HU-BTEC has established excellent industry-government-academia partnerships.    The university has state-of-the art instrumentation enabling faculty-students the opportunity to perform cutting-edge research.     Why should you join HU?  Harrisburg University offers work-oriented education in applied sciences and technology programs. Its focus is to educate career-minded individuals in the areas of science, technology, engineering, and math (STEM careers), giving them the tools to succeed, while helping to shape their communities, locally and beyond. Our goal is to help stimulate economic growth in our region by establishing a STEM educated workforce — a necessary resource in today’s economy.  At HU we believe innovation sparks success! HU is edgy, innovative, entrepreneurial, state-of-the-art, entertaining, and on the cusp of the newest, most sophisticated technological advances  With a robust and comprehensive curriculum in place, the BTEC program offers an excellent platform for educator-researchers looking to advance their careers while contributing to the HU program offerings and research.  We are looking for entrepreneurs and leaders with solid academic and research backgrounds who can shape our rapidly growing programs.     If you have the following, then we are looking for YOU:   Earned master's or doctorate from an accredited university- in any one from the following- Molecular Biotechnology, Bio-Medical Sciences, Molecular Medicine, or a related Scientific Discipline  University level teaching Experience. (online/hybrid format of teaching is preferred but not required) Ability to collaborate and be a team-member Experience in working with diverse student populations Ability to initiate and supervise interdisciplinary research with graduates and undergraduates Excellent Hands-on skills related to molecular biotechnology, nanobiotechnology or biomedical research. Excellent student evaluations at university-level teaching experience Curriculum development (preferred, but not required)",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d7d41d6e-e9f2-43e0-af0f-ac2146083d4f&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9202107521196_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "PT Faculty Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2024-10-16\n\nLocation: Philadelphia\n\nThis is on-site in our Philadelphia Campus    Harrisburg University of Science and Technology is seeking applicants for a part-time/ adjunct faculty to teach introductory and advanced undergraduate Mathematics courses for the upcoming Spring 2025 semester and beyond. Candidates should be dedicated to student-centered undergraduate teaching and should be committed to supporting the academic success of students from diverse backgrounds. Teaching is appointed on a per semester as needed basis. Responsibilities include course readiness and teaching 3 to 9 credits per semester.   Specific course needed for Spring 2025 are as follows:-  Introduction to Linear Algebra Calculus I   Minimum qualifications include a master’s degree in mathematics or in a related field.  Prior classroom teaching experience highly desirable.",
