    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d7d41d6e-e9f2-43e0-af0f-ac2146083d4f&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204284329981_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Graduate Admissions",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\n\nLocation: Harrisburg\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The Associate Director of Graduate Admissions is responsible for executing recruitment and enrollment strategies for Harrisburg University’s graduate and PhD programs within Enrollment Management. This role proactively engages prospective students across all marketing and recruitment channels and guides them through each stage of the admissions process to support established enrollment goals. __________________________________________________________________________________________ KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES Communicate the University’s graduate and PhD program offerings and value propositions to prospective students to support goals for contacts, interviews, applications, admitted students, and enrollments.  Execute recruitment strategies designed to increase enrollment in graduate and PhD programs.  Initiate and maintain relationships with prospective students and lead-generating sources across multiple communication channels, including phone, email, text, and digital platforms.  Guide prospective students through the admissions process, including follow-up on applications and ongoing counseling and support.  Review assigned prospect and applicant pipelines regularly, identify barriers to progression, and conduct timely and appropriate follow-up. In coordination with the Executive Director, program directors, and other University partners, plan and execute information sessions and recruitment (online/in-person) events to promote graduate and PhD programs.  Travel domestically and internationally, as needed, to represent the University at recruitment events or enrollment-related activities. Some evening and weekend travel may be required. Ensure accurate and complete data entry within the University’s CRM system.  Collaborate with internal partners to support development of recruitment and marketing strategies that attract and maintain a diverse student population.  Maintain detailed knowledge of academic programs, including requirements, curriculum, policies, procedures, and general institutional information.  Communicate with faculty and administration to support recruitment efforts and ensure a consistent transition from applicant to enrolled student.  Address applicant concerns, including extenuating circumstances, complaints, and appeals related to admissions decisions. Escalate policy questions, appeals, sensitive cases, and circumstances requiring exceptions to the Executive Director or appropriate University official. Ensure proper handling of confidential student information in compliance with FERPA.  Prepare regular reports related to enrollment activity, progress, observations and recommendations as needed. __________________________________________________________________________________________ Managerial Leadership Practices  Regularly meets with subordinate associates (weekly one-to-one, weekly or bi-weekly with teams) to: discuss overall business context, plans, and problems; build understanding of how their roles connect to the organization’s mission and vision; and seek feedback.  Develops and executes plans and budgets for achieving departmental/unit goals.  Assigns tasks so associates know what is required of them (quality and quantity), by when and what resources are available.  Appraises how effectively associates use their judgment and discretion in role accountabilities; creates an ongoing dialogue with them about the appraisals.  Coaches associates to increase their effectiveness and develop strengths in their role.  Continuously improves systems and processes; identifies new project opportunities.  Recommends team additions and dismissals; solicits, screens and selects candidates for consideration.  Effectively orients and trains new associates into role requirements, working relationships, company requirements and culture.  Identifies developmental opportunities for associates-once-removed.  __________________________________________________________________________________________ EXPECTATIONS OF ALL STAFF Applies best efforts and full capability each day to the work assigned by their manager.    Advises the manager when:  An assignment is not understood.    An assignment conflicts with knowledge of the circumstances, current skills, or available time/resources.    Obstacles to completing the assignment exist or are likely to occur.    Opportunities to better complete or improve the assignment exist or may occur.    Understands and demonstrates our cultural expectations. __________________________________________________________________________________________ MINIMUM ROLE REQUIREMENTS Bachelor’s degree required. Minimum of 5 years of relevant experience. Sales, student recruitment, or customer service experience required. Experience with Slate or other higher education CRM systems preferred. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and maintain consistent follow-up with prospective students. __________________________________________________________________________________________ WORK HOURS The university work week is Sunday through Saturday. Most employees are expected to work within the core hours of 8:00 am to 5:00 pm, Monday through Friday. To accommodate business needs, employees may be assigned to other workdays and/or hours, including weekends and evenings, and may be required to work overtime.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d7d41d6e-e9f2-43e0-af0f-ac2146083d4f&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204284253136_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Career Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\n\nLocation: Harrisburg\n\nThis position is 100% Grant Funded for up to four years through the Department of Education Reporting to the Assistant Director of Career Services & Employer Relations, the Career Coach serves as a key member of the Career Services & Experiential Learning team at Harrisburg University, with a primary focus on delivering comprehensive career counseling and outreach to students. This role supports students, including underrepresented and low-income groups in identifying, developing, and achieving their career goals through individualized coaching, programming, and access to experiential learning opportunities. The Career Coach works collaboratively with internal departments and external partners, including employers and alumni, to create and sustain career pathways that align with students’ academic and professional aspirations. The ideal candidate brings a strong commitment to equity and inclusion and demonstrates the ability to effectively support a diverse student population. KEY ROLE ACCOUNTABILITIES   Provide one-on-one and group career coaching to students, including career exploration, job search strategies, resume and cover letter development, and interview preparation  Deliver workshops, classroom presentations, and career-related programming to support student career readiness  Assist students in identifying and pursuing internships, apprenticeships, and other experiential learning opportunities Proactively engage students through targeted outreach strategies to increase utilization of career services  Establish and maintain relationships with employers, alumni, and community partners to expand career opportunities for students  Collaborate with faculty and program leads to align career development initiatives with academic programs Partner with faculty and program leads to assess gaps in internship availability and proactively engage employers and community partners to co-create opportunities that align with program-specific workforce needs  Assist in tracking student engagement and outcomes related to career services and experiential learning Helping to create \"streamlined programming in addition to existing services\" by connecting key personnel on collaborative initiatives REQUIREMENTS OF ALL ASSOCIATES   Applies best efforts and full capability each day to the work assigned by own manager. Advises manager when:  An assignment is not understood. An assignment conflicts with knowledge of the circumstances, current skills or available time/resources. Obstacles to completing the assignment exist or are likely to occur. Opportunities to better complete or improve the assignment exist or may occur.  Understands and demonstrates our cultural expectations. MINIMUM ROLE REQUIREMENTS Bachelor’s degree in business, leadership, human resources or related field or the equivalent work experience in career services, corporate recruitment and/or corporate/external relations preferred Experience in career coaching, advising, student services, or workforce development Excellent writing, presentation, project management and interpersonal communication skills and demonstrated ability to develop strong, collaborative relationships with colleagues, students, and employers Proficiency in Windows and Microsoft Office computer systems, experience with computer-based integrated student databases and receptive to the use of new technology while also able to utilize web and social media platforms for recruitment; knowledge of LinkedIn, Handshake, customer relationship management (Slate) and a student information system (Jenzabar or Stellic)",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d7d41d6e-e9f2-43e0-af0f-ac2146083d4f&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204316595057_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Student Library Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\n\nLocation: Harrisburg\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The Student Library Assistant provides frontline support to library patrons and assists library staff with a range of daily operations, events, and special projects. The position supports the academic mission of the Harrisburg University Library by delivering responsive patron service, maintaining collection accessibility, and contributing student perspectives to library planning and programming. __________________________________________________________________________________________ KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES Patron Services Assist library patrons by answering common questions and providing referrals, directions, and instructions. Process interlibrary loan (ILL) requests accurately and in a timely manner. Research requests for books and other materials on behalf of patrons and staff. Collection & Lending Support Assist with lending services, including shelf checks, reshelving returned materials, and inventory checks. Maintain accurate organization of physical and digital library resources in accordance with library procedures. Events & Projects Assist with planning, setup, and marketing for library events and activities. Download and organize library statistics as directed by library staff. Contribute to special projects such as resource analysis and research initiatives as assigned.   __________________________________________________________________________________________ EXPECTATIONS OF ALL STAFF Applies best efforts and full capability each day to the work assigned by their manager.    Advises the manager when:  An assignment is not understood.    An assignment conflicts with knowledge of the circumstances, current skills, or available time/resources.    Obstacles to completing the assignment exist or are likely to occur.    Opportunities to better complete or improve the assignment exist or may occur.    Understands and demonstrates our cultural expectations. _________________________________________________________________________________________ MINIMUM ROLE REQUIREMENTS Eligibility Must be a currently enrolled Harrisburg University student in good academic standing. Must be available to work on site for a minimum of 8 hours per week on a consistent schedule. Core Competencies Strong verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to assist patrons clearly and professionally. Reliability and accountability in maintaining a consistent work schedule. Attention to detail in handling materials, processing requests, and organizing information. Commitment to providing a positive experience for all library patrons.  __________________________________________________________________________________________ WORK HOURS This is an on-site position. Student Library Assistants are expected to work a minimum of 8 hours per week on a consistent schedule determined in coordination with library staff. Specific hours are assigned based on library operational needs and the student's course schedule.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d7d41d6e-e9f2-43e0-af0f-ac2146083d4f&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204316589193_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Marketing & Brand Designer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\n\nLocation: Harrisburg\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The Marketing & Brand Designer is responsible for conceptualizing, developing, and executing creative strategies and visual communications that advance the University’s brand, enrollment, engagement, and institutional priorities. This role exercises independent judgment and creative discretion in translating marketing strategy and institutional messaging into compelling visual concepts and integrated campaign materials across digital and print platforms.  Working under the direction of the Director of Marketing & Digital Experience and in close collaboration with Communications, this position leads the creative development of high-visibility campaigns and institutional initiatives while helping shape and maintain the University’s visual identity and brand standards. __________________________________________________________________________________________ KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES Conceptualize and develop original visual solutions that support institutional marketing strategy, enrollment goals, and audience engagement.  Lead creative direction and visual execution for integrated marketing campaigns and high-visibility institutional initiatives.  Exercise independent judgment in the interpretation and application of University brand standards, visual identity, typography, layout, and storytelling approaches.  Design and oversee the development of marketing and communications materials across digital, print, web, social media, advertising, and recruitment platforms.  Collaborate with Marketing and Communications leadership to translate strategic priorities into compelling creative concepts and audience-focused messaging.  Help define, evolve, and maintain the University’s visual identity, design systems, and brand consistency across channels and audiences.  Evaluate creative effectiveness and recommend design approaches that strengthen engagement, user experience, and campaign performance.  Manage multiple concurrent creative projects in a fast-paced environment while maintaining high standards for quality, innovation, and timeliness.  Provide creative guidance and coordination with internal collaborators and external vendors to ensure alignment with institutional objectives and brand standards. Preferred experience with photography and media production, including capturing and editing visual content to support marketing, brand, social media, and recruitment initiatives. __________________________________________________________________________________________ EXPECTATIONS OF ALL STAFF Applies best efforts and full capability each day to the work assigned by their manager.    Advises the manager when:  An assignment is not understood.    An assignment conflicts with knowledge of the circumstances, current skills, or available time/resources.    Obstacles to completing the assignment exist or are likely to occur.    Opportunities to better complete or improve the assignment exist or may occur.    Understands and demonstrates our cultural expectations. _________________________________________________________________________________________ MINIMUM ROLE REQUIREMENTS Conceptualize and develop original visual solutions that support institutional marketing strategy, enrollment goals, and audience engagement.  Lead creative direction and visual execution for integrated marketing campaigns and high-visibility institutional initiatives.  Exercise independent judgment in the interpretation and application of University brand standards, visual identity, typography, layout, and storytelling approaches.  Design and oversee the development of marketing and communications materials across digital, print, web, social media, advertising, and recruitment platforms.  Collaborate with Marketing and Communications leadership to translate strategic priorities into compelling creative concepts and audience-focused messaging.  Help define, evolve, and maintain the University’s visual identity, design systems, and brand consistency across channels and audiences.  Evaluate creative effectiveness and recommend design approaches that strengthen engagement, user experience, and campaign performance.  Manage multiple concurrent creative projects in a fast-paced environment while maintaining high standards for quality, innovation, and timeliness.  Provide creative guidance and coordination with internal collaborators and external vendors to ensure alignment with institutional objectives and brand standards. Preferred experience with photography and media production, including capturing and editing visual content to support marketing, brand, social media, and recruitment initiatives. __________________________________________________________________________________________ WORK HOURS The university work week is Sunday through Saturday. Employees are expected to work within the core hours of 8:00 am to 5:00 pm, Monday through Friday. To accommodate business needs, employees may be assigned to other workdays and/or hours, including weekends and evenings, and may be required to work overtime.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d7d41d6e-e9f2-43e0-af0f-ac2146083d4f&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204316546912_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Jr Lab Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\n\nLocation: Harrisburg\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The Junior Lab Assistant supports the academic science programs in Biology and Chemistry at Harrisburg University. Working under the direction of assigned faculty, the Junior Lab Assistant provides hands-on lab preparation and maintenance support that enables the successful delivery of undergraduate science courses. Specific duties vary by week depending on the course being supported and the student's level of experience. __________________________________________________________________________________________ KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES Lab Preparation & Maintenance Set up and break down lab materials before and after each assigned course session. Wash, dry, and properly store glassware and lab equipment following established safety and handling procedures. Label lab ware accurately in preparation for scheduled lab activities. Prepare solutions, buffers, and growth media as directed by the assigned faculty member. Maintain accurate inventories of chemicals and supplies, notifying the faculty supervisor when stock is low or materials need to be reordered. General Support Complete errands and light office tasks in support of the department as needed. Coordinate with the assigned faculty member on scheduling, priorities, and any changes to lab setup requirements. __________________________________________________________________________________________ EXPECTATIONS OF ALL STAFF Applies best efforts and full capability each day to the work assigned by their manager.    Advises the manager when:  An assignment is not understood.    An assignment conflicts with knowledge of the circumstances, current skills, or available time/resources.    Obstacles to completing the assignment exist or are likely to occur.    Opportunities to better complete or improve the assignment exist or may occur.    Understands and demonstrates our cultural expectations. __________________________________________________________________________________________ MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Eligibility Must be a currently enrolled Harrisburg University student in good academic standing. Must be available to work variable hours across the work week as course schedules require. Academic Preparation Must have completed at least one semester of a general Biology course with a grade of C or better for Biology lab support positions. Must have completed at least one semester of a general Chemistry course with a grade of C or better for Chemistry lab support positions. Core Competencies Punctual, reliable, and organized, with the ability to follow detailed instructions consistently. Ability to work carefully and safely in a lab environment, handling equipment and materials with appropriate care. Ability to work independently on assigned tasks while staying aligned with faculty direction. _________________________________________________________________________________________ WORK HOURS Hours vary each week based on course schedules and lab preparation needs. Student workers must be available at various times during the work week as determined by the assigned faculty member and approved by the Chair of the Department of Integrated Sciences.",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
